agent_prs.body:
The live UAT issue was caused by the report workflow reusing a stale or partial journal source when an account was selected, which dropped posted history and could leak rows from the wrong account into the General Ledger and Account Statement. The fix keeps account filtering applied consistently to both report views while reading from the authenticated full journal set.

- Summary
  - Selecting an account should narrow the ledger/statement to that account’s posted journals without losing the underlying data source.
  - Switching accounts must not reuse rows from a previously selected account or render stale closing balances.

- Changes
  - Reused the authenticated full-journal report source when building the selected-account ledger/statement view instead of relying on a partial or stale snapshot.
  - Added business/account validation around the selection effect so stale selections are ignored and ledger/statement state is cleared when the chosen account is invalid or absent.
  - Applied the selected account consistently to both General Ledger and Account Statement so their totals and transactions are derived from the same report source.
  - Added regression coverage to ensure selected-account changes do not leak another account’s posted rows into the current table.

- Example
```tsx
if (!businessId || !reportSource || reportSource.businessId !== businessId) {
  setLedger(null);
  setStatement(null);
  return;
}

const input = { businessId, accountId: selectedAccountId, dateFrom, dateTo };
setLedger(reportSource.service.getGeneralLedger(input));
setStatement(reportSource.service.getAccountStatement(input));
```

This keeps the selected account scoped to the correct journal data while preventing stale rows from a different account from being rendered.

