### What happened

A Symbol's `type_info` gives only the feature's own `: T` typing. A feature that gets its type by subsetting, reference subsetting or redefinition reports no type. A feature that has its own typing and also subsets another feature reports only its own type. Reference subsetting (`::>`) is not in `specializations` either, so nothing in the Symbol says where `pRef` gets its type.

```sysml
package P {
    part def T;
    part def V;
    part def Owner {
        part q : T;
        part pSub :> q;             // subsetting
        ref part pRef ::> q;        // reference subsetting
        part pBoth : V :> q;        // typing and subsetting
        attribute a : ScalarValues::Real;
    }
    part def SubOwner :> Owner {
        part :>> q;                 // redefinition
    }
    part tuned : Owner {
        attribute :>> a = 3.5;      // redefinition with a value
    }
}
```

